<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.2 · Varlamore, Wyrmscraig & Runecraft" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-2" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.2</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Varlamore, Wyrmscraig &amp; Runecraft</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Let quest XP do the heavy lifting: fight the Moons, visit modern Wyrmscraig, and step Runecraft through 47 → 50 → 52 → 55 while quests repeatedly shrink the next gap.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Perilous Moons → Heart of Darkness → Slayer 60 → Runecraft 47 → Fallen From Grace → Crafting 65 → Runecraft 50 → Devious Minds → Runecraft 52 → Final Dawn → Runecraft 55 → Fremennik Exiles."
        stats={["Claim each quest's XP before training for the next quest", "Unboosted 60 Slayer, 65 Crafting and 55 Runecraft before The Fremennik Exiles", "Save the training to Runecraft 60, Slayer 69 and Crafting 70 for later quests"]}
        unlocks={["Neypotzli and its first normal Lunar Chest reward", "Wyrmscraig, Tapoyauik and the Varlamore finale", "Island of Stone and V's shield"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Before starting:</strong> you should have completed While Guthix Sleeps, Twilight's Promise, Children of the Sun and Pandemonium, and built your camphor-hulled skiff. Check for at least 58 Slayer, 67 Magic, 60 Strength, 70 Prayer and Defence with Piety, roughly 63 Crafting and 38 Runecraft, 67 Sailing, 71 Mining, 70 Smithing and 65 Fishing. Claim WGS's Thieving, Farming, Herblore and Hunter rewards if you have not already. Your levels may be higher, especially if you used Barbarian Fishing for Agility. Keep using your Barrows gloves, dragon defender, Helm of Neitiznot and Proselyte; a black mask or Bowfa is optional.</div>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Make the most of quest Runecraft XP:</strong> train to the next quest's required level, complete it and claim its reward before training again. Perilous Moons, Fallen From Grace, Devious Minds, The Final Dawn and The Fremennik Exiles award <strong>5,000 + 5,000 + 5,000 + 25,000 + 30,000 = 70,000 Runecraft XP</strong> across this chapter. You need each quest's entry level before receiving its reward. Training to 60 can wait until the later quest that needs it.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Varlamore · two quests before Slayer</div><h2>Take the large quest rewards before training.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i32-moons" number="1" title="Complete Perilous Moons and claim one normal Lunar Chest reward">
        <p>You already meet the requirements: unboosted 48 Slayer, 20 Hunter, 20 Fishing, 20 Runecraft, 10 Construction and Twilight's Promise. Go to the <strong>Cam Torum entrance on the south side of Ralos' Rise</strong> in Varlamore, then follow the Cam Torum path into <strong>Neypotzli</strong>. Speak to Zuma/Attala at the entrance to begin. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Perilous_Moons" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest requirements and rewards</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Supply check:</strong> a <strong>big fishing net, knife, pestle and mortar, and rope</strong> are available in Neypotzli's supply crates. Collect them before preparing local food and moonlight potions.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Neypotzli supplies replace a potion-shopping detour" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Take the <strong>big fishing net and knife from a fishing-supplies crate</strong>, the <strong>pestle and mortar from a herblore-supplies crate</strong>, and the <strong>rope from a hunting-supplies crate</strong>. Use the nearby fishing spots and cooking facilities for the quest's food; hunting is another local food option. Moonlight grubs and the campsite's potion supplies make moonlight potions inside the dungeon. Refill these supplies between Moons and save your ranarrs for other fights.</p>
          <p>These are reusable gathering tools. If you leave the dungeon or restart, collect any missing tools from the crates again and prepare fresh food/potions before entering a boss room. Keep the ordinary combat gear listed below; the supplies do not replace defensive equipment.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>First trip:</strong> bring the banked dragon scimitar, dragon defender, Barrows gloves, Helm of Neitiznot, your best <em>defensive</em> melee armour, food and a teleport. Neypotzli has campsite crates, fishing and hunting resources, cooking stoves, and moonlight grubs to turn into moonlight potions, so the ordinary loop is <strong>gather/cook food → make potions → fight each Moon → open the chest</strong>. Moonlight potions restore Prayer and boost combat; protection prayers <strong>do not reduce the Moon bosses' attacks</strong>. Their three-hit sequences punish poor defence, so defensive armour and learning the special phases matter more than a rare damage upgrade. Piety is useful, but not a substitute for movement. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Moons_of_Peril/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current encounter strategy</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="The three Moons, using attainable weapons" label="Boss primer">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Blood Moon—slash:</strong> use the dragon scimitar and defender. Hits on you heal her; prioritize defence, follow Eyatlalli's highlighted safe circle, move off raining-blood pools and work the highlighted blood-jaguar phase rather than trying to out-DPS mistakes.</li>
            <li><strong>Blue Moon—crush:</strong> a <strong>dragon mace</strong> can be bought at the Heroes' Guild after Heroes' Quest for a crush weapon; if you already have a reasonable crush weapon, use it. Punch the ice block to recover your frozen weapon while avoiding spikes; during the other special, relight both braziers while avoiding tornadoes.</li>
            <li><strong>Eclipse Moon—stab:</strong> use a banked stab-capable weapon, including the dragon dagger if owned; the dragon scimitar can still finish the quest if no special swap is available. Keep the moving moon shield between you and the boss during the ray phase, and face each spawning clone during the mimic phase.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>You can leave and restock between encounters. No Barrows set, Moon gear or Bowfa is required.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Defeat all three as the quest directs and collect its <strong>one normal Lunar Chest reward</strong>. Claim <strong>40,000 Slayer, 5,000 Runecraft, 5,000 Hunter and 5,000 Fishing XP</strong>. Bank any Moon unique, including an Eclipse atlatl, as a welcome bonus; <strong>do not farm a set</strong>. If you started at exactly 58 Slayer, <strong>224,466 + 40,000 = 264,466 XP</strong>, leaving <strong>9,276 XP</strong> to level 60 <em>before</em> the next quest's Slayer reward. Check your Slayer XP, then complete the next quest before training.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-heart" number="2" title="Complete The Heart of Darkness while in Varlamore">
        <p>Begin with <strong>Prince Itzla at the Teomat</strong>. You already have Twilight's Promise and the unboosted 55 Mining, 48 Thieving, 48 Slayer and 46 Agility needed; Perilous Moons is not a direct prerequisite, but both stories are required later for The Final Dawn. Investigate the cult, travel into the icy ruins of <strong>Tapoyauik</strong> and defeat <strong>Amoxliatl</strong>. Bring <strong>30 coins</strong>, melee gear, the dragon mace/defender if purchased, food, <strong>two Prayer potions as an initial supply</strong>, and an emergency teleport; use Protect from Magic in the fight. During the fight, move off persistent ice, destroy unstable ice blocks with melee before they burst/heal her, and reactivate Protect from Magic when her icicle attack switches Prayer off. You can move on after completing the quest; returning to fight Amoxliatl is optional. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Heart_of_Darkness" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest walkthrough and rewards</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Amoxliatl/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fight mechanics</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="The rented room and the fight's Prayer supply" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>The <strong>30 coins pay the bartender in Quetzacalli Gorge for the basement room</strong>; carry them before the investigation starts. For the boss, make only the missing Prayer-potion doses using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer-potion recipe and ingredient recovery</a>. Start with two potions and adjust after an attempt if you need more.</p>
          <p>The investigation supplies the <strong>emissary robes</strong>. Keep the complete outfit for The Final Dawn; if it is later missing, the chest at the Tower of Ascension supplies a replacement.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Claim <strong>8,000 XP each in Mining, Thieving, Slayer and Agility</strong> and the Tapoyauik access. If you started Perilous Moons at exactly 58 Slayer, <strong>224,466 + 40,000 + 8,000 = 272,466 XP</strong>. Level 60 begins at <strong>273,742 XP</strong>, leaving at most <strong>1,276 XP</strong>; Duradel's notes or other tasks may have brought you closer.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-slayer-60" number="3" title="Finish any remaining training to 60 Slayer">
        <p>Check your Slayer level <strong>after both Varlamore quest rewards</strong> and any Duradel's notes you used. Even if you started at exactly 58, you need at most <strong>1,276 more XP</strong>; you may already be 60. If short, complete ordinary Slayer assignments through a master you can use and <strong>stop at 60</strong>. Wear a black mask if you obtained one in Chapter 3.1. <strong>The Fremennik Exiles</strong> needs unboosted 60 Slayer and awards 50,000 XP afterward, so leave the training to 69 for later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Runecraft · prepare for Fallen From Grace</div><h2>Reach 47, then visit Wyrmscraig.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-47" number="4" title="Reach 47 Runecraft after the Moon reward">
        <p>Check your Runecraft XP after Perilous Moons' <strong>5,000 XP</strong>. If you had about <strong>33,210 XP</strong> from earlier chapters, you now have about <strong>38,210 XP</strong>. Level 47 begins at <strong>75,127 XP</strong>, leaving approximately <strong>36,917 XP</strong> to train in that example. You need less if you already earned more XP. <strong>Stop at an unboosted 47</strong> for Fallen From Grace.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i32-rc-methods" skill="Runecraft" target="47 now; return for each later quest level" why="Short sessions between quests let their rewards reduce the remaining training." recommended="Guardians of the Rift: gather fragments, make guardian essence, enter opened altars, craft runes, then use charged cells to reinforce barriers or make guardians. Balance elemental/catalytic energy for reward searches; you can focus entirely on the minigame." relaxed="Sins of the Father opens the Daeyalt mine in Darkmeyer. Mine shards with longer, quieter clicks; exchange them for banked essence, then use it at Ourania/ZMI. Mining is relaxed, though the bank and altar laps still need attention." informational={true} />
        <p><strong>GOTR refresher:</strong> return to the Temple of the Eye beneath the Wizards' Tower (completed in Chapter 1), enter the Rift, mine guardian fragments, convert them at the workbench, and take essence through whichever rune altar portal is open. Deposit crafted guardian stones into the Great Guardian and place charged cells in barrier/guardian positions so the rift closes. Earn elemental and catalytic points and search the Rewards Guardian between games. Keep any essence pouches from reward searches. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Guardians_of_the_Rift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Minigame and reward mechanics</a>. For a quieter split, <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ourania_Altar" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ourania</a> is west of the Battlefield: bring pure/daeyalt essence and 20 expendable runes per bank access, use the longer safe east path if desired, then craft mixed runes at its altar. Mining Daeyalt is the relaxed portion; the bank/altar loop is not truly AFK. Do not farm a pouch early solely for Step 8.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-fallen" number="5" title="Complete Fallen From Grace using your own camphor skiff">
        <p><strong>Requirements:</strong> unboosted 62 Sailing, 60 Crafting, <strong>47 Runecraft</strong>, 53 Mining and Pandemonium. With the Runecraft training above, you are ready to start. Sail your <strong>own raft or skiff—not a sloop</strong> to <strong>Wyrmscraig</strong>, south-west of Charred Island. Your Chapter 2 <strong>camphor-hulled skiff</strong> works. Wyrmscraig is a newer player-designed island; the main settlement is <strong>Auchrie</strong>. Speak with <strong>Cormac in its central hut</strong> and follow the missing-villager/sunstone investigation. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fallen_From_Grace" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest guide</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Tools on the island; food and potions before the crossing" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>The island's <strong>south-east coastal tent</strong> supplies the pickaxe, hammer and chisel, and the investigation provides its special materials, including sunstone. Bring banked tools if convenient, or collect replacements after landing.</p>
          <p>Bank before boarding your camphor skiff: your combat food and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer/stat-restoration supplies</a> must come from the mainland until the quest opens the island bank. An ordinary restore does not replace a Prayer potion. If supplies run short, sail back to restock before another fight.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Bank before departure:</strong> you cannot use a Wyrmscraig bank or teleport to the island until the quest is complete. Bring melee gear, a <strong>crush</strong> option such as the Heroes' Guild dragon mace, food, Prayer/restore supplies and a return teleport before sailing; leave room for quest items. A pickaxe, hammer and chisel are supplied by the <strong>tent on Wyrmscraig's south-east coast</strong>; search it for each missing tool. You can sail back to restock if needed—just budget the return crossing.</div>
        <p>Investigate the monolith and cavern, defeat the three trolls (Protect from Melee helps in their multicombat area), solve the cathedral trail and face the <strong>weaker quest version of the Mad Angel</strong>. It is a mechanics fight: use crush and Protect from Melee for ordinary attacks, move through/behind her telegraphed sword sweep, step onto the marked shadows to redirect the yellow orb, and switch to Protect from Magic for the blue lightning. This is not the repeatable post-quest boss farm. Claim <strong>12,500 Sailing, 10,000 Crafting, 5,000 Mining and 5,000 Runecraft XP</strong> plus Wyrmscraig travel, Golem Crafting, Mortimer's Slayer-master access and the repeatable Mad Angel unlock.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="What can wait on Wyrmscraig" label="Optional after the quest">
          <p>You can return later for <strong>Hallowfell</strong> equipment from the repeat boss, <strong>Sunstone Golem Crafting</strong>, or <strong>Mortimer's</strong> Slayer assignments if eligible. All are optional here. For the next step's 65 Crafting, use materials you already have if that is convenient.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-craft-65" number="6" title="Reach 65 Crafting after Fallen From Grace">
        <p>Check your Crafting XP <strong>after Fallen's 10,000 XP</strong>. If you started at exactly level 63, <strong>368,599 + 10,000 = 378,599 XP</strong>; level 65 begins at <strong>449,428 XP</strong>, leaving <strong>70,829 XP</strong> to train. You may need much less. Use materials from your bank and <strong>stop at an unboosted 65</strong> for <strong>The Fremennik Exiles</strong>. That quest awards 50,000 Crafting XP, so complete it before training to 70 for Monkey Madness II.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i32-craft-methods" skill="Crafting" target="65, unboosted" why="The Fremennik Exiles needs 65 Crafting and awards another 50,000 XP afterward." recommended="Blow banked molten glass into useful lantern lenses or other available products; use banked gems and battlestaff materials where they make sense." relaxed="For fresh glass, gather/buy buckets of sand and soda ash or cook seaweed, combine one of each at a furnace, then use a glassblowing pipe. Make enough to reach 65 from your current XP." informational={true} />
        <p><strong>Making glass:</strong> Superglass Make requires <strong>77 Magic</strong>. If you are still around the 67 Magic reached earlier, use an ordinary furnace instead. Keep <strong>one molten glass</strong> banked for The Fremennik Exiles.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-50" number="7" title="Reach 50 Runecraft and obtain a pouch for Devious Minds">
        <p>Check your Runecraft XP after Fallen's <strong>5,000 XP</strong>. If Step 4 stopped exactly at 47's <strong>75,127 XP</strong>, you now have at least <strong>80,127 XP</strong>; level 50 begins at <strong>101,333 XP</strong>, leaving at most <strong>21,206 XP</strong>. Return to your chosen method and <strong>stop at an unboosted 50</strong>. Complete Devious Minds for its reward before training to 52.</p>
        <p><strong>Find a pouch for Devious Minds:</strong> check your bank and inventory for a <strong>non-degraded large essence pouch or colossal pouch</strong>. If absent, first search any saved GOTR reward pulls. Pouch drops follow ownership progression: hold a <strong>small pouch</strong> (the Abyss dark mage can give one), then <strong>medium</strong>, then <strong>large</strong>—check the bank after each. Temple of the Eye may already have supplied the medium. GOTR's Rewards Guardian can award pouches naturally; alternatively, fairy ring <strong>ALR</strong> reaches the Abyssal Area <em>without a Wilderness crossing</em>. Kill ordinary Abyssal walkers/guardians there with combat gear, food and teleport until the missing next pouch drops. The August 2026 improvement raised pouch rolls to <strong>up to 1/5 per walker</strong> or <strong>up to 1/8 per guardian</strong> (formerly 1/42); those are <em>odds, not a guaranteed number of kills</em>. You do not need the pouch's use level to obtain it. Repair a degraded large pouch through the dark mage before the quest. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Essence_pouch" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Pouch order and sources</a> · <a href="https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/summer-sweep-up---agility--chambers-of-xeric-changes?oldschool=1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex's August 2026 pouch-rate update</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Classic detour · then back to Varlamore</div><h2>Each quest makes the next Runecraft interval shorter.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i32-devious" number="8" title="Complete Devious Minds and claim 5,000 Runecraft XP">
        <p>Check for <strong>50 Runecraft without a boost</strong>, 65 Smithing, 50 Fletching, Wanted!, Troll Stronghold/Death Plateau, Doric's Quest and Enter the Abyss. The route covers these. Obtain a <strong>mithril two-handed sword</strong> (buy from <strong>Gaius in Taverley</strong> or smith it), <strong>bow string</strong> and the <strong>non-degraded large or colossal pouch</strong>. Speak to the monk outside Paterdomus, use Doric's whetstone on the sword, attach the string and follow the orb/Entrana phase. The sword and string are consumed. A normal large pouch is consumed; a colossal pouch survives. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Devious_Minds/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current item and phase guide</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="The sword, string and consumable pouch" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>If you have no mithril two-handed sword banked, buy <strong>one from Gaius's Two-Handed Shop in Taverley</strong>. Pick <strong>one flax in the Seers' Village flax field</strong> and spin it into <strong>one bow string</strong> at a spinning wheel (10 Crafting). Select bow string, not the separate Sailing linen-yarn product.</p>
          <p>Follow the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-2/#i32-rc-50`}>pouch instructions above</a> if you have no suitable pouch, and repair it before departure. Keep it for the quest's orb phase: an ordinary large pouch is consumed. Search any saved Guardians of the Rift rewards before hunting for a replacement.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Ironman travel warning:</strong> bank weapons and armour for Entrana before the Law Altar trip. The quest's Abyss entry via the Mage of Zamorak crosses <strong>level 4–7 Wilderness</strong>; ALR is useful for <em>pouch farming</em> but does not replace this quest phase. A Hardcore Ironman should treat the crossing as real PvP risk: travel light, check the world, and use a teleport/escape plan. Do not insert the orb into the pouch before you are ready for that phase; losing it can require recovery. Finish with Sir Tiffy and claim <strong>5,000 Runecraft, 5,000 Fletching and 6,500 Smithing XP</strong>. This also closes a later Secrets of the North / Desert Treasure II prerequisite.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-52" number="9" title="Reach 52 Runecraft after Devious Minds">
        <p>Check your Runecraft XP after Devious Minds' <strong>5,000 XP</strong>. If you stopped training at exactly level 50, <strong>101,333 + 5,000 = 106,333 XP</strong>. Level 52 begins at <strong>123,660 XP</strong>, leaving at most <strong>17,327 XP</strong>. Use your preferred method and <strong>stop at an unboosted 52</strong> for The Final Dawn. Claim its 25,000-XP reward before training to 55.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-dawn" number="10" title="Complete The Final Dawn and claim its 25,000 Runecraft XP">
        <p><strong>Requirements:</strong> Perilous Moons, The Heart of Darkness and unboosted <strong>66 Thieving, 52 Runecraft and 52 Fletching</strong>. WGS and Chapter 2 covered Thieving and Fletching; the training above finishes Runecraft. Start with <strong>Servius in the Sunrise Palace</strong>. Pack the complete <strong>emissary robes</strong>, a knife, <strong>one ordinary bone</strong>, and ordinary food/combat supplies. Beer and the puzzle's other special ingredients are supplied during the relevant phases. This is a long Varlamore story/fight sequence, so <strong>bank and regear between phases</strong> instead of hauling every item at once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Final_Dawn" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest and combat walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Recover the robes and reserve one bone" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>If the emissary outfit is missing, search the <strong>chest at the south of the Tower of Ascension, south of Salvager Overlook</strong>; leave four spaces for its pieces. Buy a missing knife from the <strong>Lumbridge general store</strong>. Kill a chicken, cow or goblin near Lumbridge for <strong>one ordinary bone</strong> and keep it for the dog; this avoids relying on a spare combat-food item being accepted.</p>
          <p>Take the beer from the <strong>upstairs Cam Torum pub</strong> for Galna. The basement's <strong>south-west cabinet</strong> supplies the drinks used in the subsequent puzzle; a banked brewing collection is unnecessary. For the longer fights, refill through the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>ordinary potion supply route</a> between phases.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <ExpandableNote title="Prepare for several encounters and two different finales" label="Fight plan">
          <p>Use the existing dragon scimitar/defender, Helm of Neitiznot, Barrows gloves, defensive armour, Piety, Prayer/restore potions, good food, an emergency teleport, and a <strong>Ranged weapon and ammunition from your bank</strong> plus Ava's accumulator. No Bowfa, Eclipse atlatl, Moon set, black mask, Fire Cape or Rigour is required; a Moon drop is merely a bonus.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Emissary Enforcer, Chimalli/Lucius and cultist waves:</strong> expect multiple fights, changing threats and ground/projectile mechanics. Protect against the active attack style, move from telegraphs, clear adds and restock when a phase ends.</li>
            <li><strong>Ennius Tullus:</strong> he has <strong>Protect from Ranged and Magic simultaneously</strong>, so this is a <strong>melee</strong> fight. Keep a protection prayer up for his ordinary attacks and step onto the safe circles/away from marked sunfire attacks; do not waste supplies trying to range through his prayers.</li>
            <li><strong>Augur Metzli:</strong> now Ranged is useful. She starts in a ranged-attacking form, later alternates Ranged/Magic after sweeper attacks; switch the matching protection prayer and move through safe rows/columns or white portals for waves and sweepers. During the final quadrant/fire phase, keep moving through the portal to the safe quadrant while attacking when possible. Prince Itzla assists, but you still handle your own mechanics.</li>
          </ul>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Finish and claim <strong>55,000 Thieving, 25,000 Runecraft and 25,000 Fletching XP</strong>, plus the selectable <strong>55,000 combat-XP lamp</strong> (a skill of at least level 40, including Prayer), the <strong>Arkan blade</strong> and access to the Crypt of Tonali/Doom of Mokhaiotl. <strong>Put the one lamp into Ranged by default:</strong> the next quest needs unboosted 62 Ranged, and the later Fire Cape preparation aims around 75–80. If you start at exactly 60 Ranged, <strong>273,742 + 55,000 = 328,742 XP</strong>; level 62 starts at <strong>333,804 XP</strong>, leaving just <strong>5,062 XP</strong> to train. If optional play has already put Ranged comfortably around Fire-Cape readiness, choose <strong>Magic instead</strong> toward the later 75 Magic needed for Dragon Slayer II and Desert Treasure II. Choose one skill for this lamp. The Arkan blade requires <strong>60 Attack</strong> and offers useful stab/slash and a special attack, but its <strong>64 Strength bonus</strong> is slightly below the dragon scimitar's 66; it is <em>not</em> a universal replacement. No post-quest Delve farm is required. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Arkan_blade" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Blade stats</a>. <strong>Claim the 25,000 RC XP before Step 11.</strong></p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-55" number="11" title="Reach 55 Runecraft after The Final Dawn">
        <p>Check your Runecraft XP after the <strong>25,000-XP</strong> reward. If you stopped at exactly level 52, <strong>123,660 + 25,000 = 148,660 XP</strong>. Level 55 begins at <strong>166,636 XP</strong>, leaving at most <strong>17,976 XP</strong>. Train from your current XP and <strong>stop at an unboosted 55</strong> for <strong>The Fremennik Exiles</strong>. That quest awards another 30,000 Runecraft XP; leave the training to 60 for later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Fremennik finale</div><h2>Return to Rellekka with the skills you need.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Before leaving for Rellekka:</strong> check for unboosted <strong>65 Crafting, 60 Slayer, 60 Smithing, 60 Fishing and 55 Runecraft</strong>. Chapter 2 covered Smithing and Fishing; the training above covers the other three. You also need The Fremennik Isles, Lunar Diplomacy, Mountain Daughter and Heroes' Quest, including their prerequisites. <strong>Mining the three lunar ores needs 60 Mining, which can be boosted.</strong> Bringing three lunar bars skips that Mining check.</div>
      <RouteStep id="i32-exiles" number="12" title="Complete The Fremennik Exiles and claim its skill rewards">
        <p><strong>Before speaking to Brundt</strong> in the Rellekka Longhall, buy <strong>two kegs of beer</strong> from Thora; her Rellekka stock is not available during the exile phase. Stage the other items by phase: a <strong>mirror shield</strong> and one-handed combat weapon for the early basilisk; <strong>pet rock</strong> (reclaim from Askeladden if missing), <strong>ice gloves and fishing rod</strong> for the Mountain Camp geyser; and <strong>one molten glass, 100 astral runes, seal of passage, hammer and glassblowing pipe</strong> for Lunar Isle's lunar glass and restored V's shield. Count astrals <em>after</em> prior Lunar spells and purchases; if short, <strong>Baba Yaga's rune shop on Lunar Isle</strong> sells them, so buy only the deficit before this phase. Supply <strong>three lunar bars</strong> from the bank if owned, or bring a <strong>pickaxe</strong> and mine the three lunar ores during the quest; only the mining choice checks boostable 60 Mining. Bring food, Prayer restores and a teleport for combat. Bank between the Rellekka, Mountain Camp and Lunar phases rather than carrying all of this at once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Fremennik_Exiles" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current item and fight guide</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Recover the small tools before exile" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Buy the <strong>mirror shield from a Slayer equipment shop</strong> and an ordinary <strong>fishing rod from Gerrant in Port Sarim</strong>. If ice gloves are missing, take a pickaxe through the White Wolf Mountain boulder route and defeat the <strong>Ice Queen</strong> for another pair; the route already clears its 50-Mining obstacle. Banked <strong>smiths gloves (i)</strong> also work, but plain smiths gloves do not. No Giants' Foundry outfit grind is required.</p>
          <p>Reclaim the <strong>seal of passage from Brundt before starting the exile</strong>, and the pet rock from Askeladden. Buy the two kegs from Thora now. For the <strong>one molten glass and glassblowing pipe</strong>, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/#i31-wgs`}>WGS glass-material recovery</a> if the Crafting reserve or pipe is missing. This glass is separate from the glass already consumed by WGS.</p>
          <p>If three lunar bars are not banked, mine <strong>three lunar ores in the Lunar Isle mine</strong>, smelt them at any available furnace and use a hammer at an anvil to make the sigil as directed. Buy only the missing part of the <strong>100-astral-rune</strong> stock from Baba Yaga. For combat, <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions plus ordinary restore potions</a> are accessible separate supplies; banked super restores can save slots.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Do not confuse the required Fremennik shield with the Neitiznot shield.</strong> Check your bank for the untradeable Fremennik shield first. If absent, after the quest exiles you, take Jarvald's boat to Waterbirth Island and obtain one <em>without a drop roll</em> from <strong>Bardur</strong> deep in the dungeon: buy about <strong>5–10 rune thrownaxes</strong> from the Ranging Guild's Tribal Weapon Salesman (you have its required 40 Ranged), take your pet rock, combat gear, food and Prayer, put the rock on one floor plate and stand on the other, then use the thrownaxe special attack on the western door supports to open the lower route. Bardur gives a shield free once with an activated <strong>ring of charos(a)</strong>, or sells it for <strong>150,000 coins</strong>. A random shield from dagannoths/market guards also works, but no drop is assumed. The shield, lunar glass, enchanted V sigil and polishing rock become <strong>V's shield</strong> with a glassblowing pipe. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Waterbirth_Island_Dungeon" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Solo dungeon route</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Jormungand primer:</strong> wear the quest-made <strong>V's shield</strong>; without it, the fight's stat drain and repeated damage are severe. A dragon mace is an attainable crush option against its slight crush weakness, with ordinary defensive melee gear and Piety. <strong>Protect from Magic</strong> greatly reduces regular magic damage but does not make you invulnerable. When the screen turns red, <strong>face away</strong> from Jormungand to avoid the gaze/drain; if encased in stone, repeatedly attempt to attack to break free before the large delayed hit. Bring enough food and restore doses for a multi-minute fight; teleporting out is safer than gambling a low-supply finish. A death/teleport restarts the Jormungand fight (not the whole quest), and Brundt handles item recovery on the island. No RNG weapon is a prerequisite.</p>
        <p>Claim <strong>50,000 Slayer, 50,000 Crafting and 30,000 Runecraft XP</strong>, V's shield and Island of Stone access. The quest unlocks Basilisk Knights on task and the <strong>Neitiznot faceguard</strong> upgrade path, but the basilisk jaw is an RNG drop; keep using the already-owned Helm of Neitiznot and <strong>do not camp a jaw</strong>. If you entered the quest at its minimum levels, your new totals are Slayer <strong>273,742 + 50,000 = 323,742 XP</strong> (at least level 61), Crafting <strong>449,428 + 50,000 = 499,428 XP</strong> (at least level 66), and Runecraft <strong>166,636 + 30,000 = 196,636 XP</strong> (at least level 56). Check your new levels before continuing. Training to Slayer 69, Crafting 70 and Runecraft 60 comes later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.2 complete · new islands and quest rewards</div>
        <h3>You are ready to prepare for the Fight Caves.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Complete:</strong> Perilous Moons (including one normal Lunar Chest reward), The Heart of Darkness, Fallen From Grace, Devious Minds, The Final Dawn and The Fremennik Exiles.</li>
          <li><strong>Training complete:</strong> 60 Slayer, 65 Crafting and Runecraft 47 → 50 → 52 → 55, with quest rewards between sessions to shorten each return.</li>
          <li><strong>Rewards:</strong> Wyrmscraig and Tapoyauik access, Island of Stone, V's shield, Arkan blade, and Exiles' additional 50,000 Slayer / 50,000 Crafting / 30,000 Runecraft XP. Check your new levels before the next chapter.</li>
          <li><strong>For later:</strong> the Fire Cape and training to Runecraft 60, Slayer 69 and Crafting 70 come in later chapters. Moon armour or atlatl, Hallowfell, Mad Angel drops, black mask/Slayer helmet, basilisk jaw/faceguard and Bowfa/crystal remain optional upgrades.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
